{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "mma m16n8k8: D = A B + C on a warp's fragments as PTX's mma.sync.aligned.m16n8k8.row.col lays them out, f16 A and B, f32 C and D, 32 lanes, under gt1030 (1768 dataflows tried)\n  each of D's 128 elements is a sum of 8 products of f16 and its C\n   1. 176       output-stationary; A: 12 xor shuffles (unpacked); B: 16 shuffles (unpacked); k order by lane, depth 8\n   2. 186       output-stationary; A: 12 xor shuffles (unpacked); B: 8 shuffles; k order by lane, depth 8\n   3. 188       output-stationary; A: 6 xor shuffles; B: 16 shuffles (unpacked); k order by lane, depth 8\n   4. 192       A-stationary; B: 16 shuffles (unpacked); partial sums: 12 xor shuffles, depth 4\n   5. 192       blocked (a lane: 2 rows x 8 columns x 2 of k); B: 16 shuffles (unpacked); partial sums: 12 xor shuffles, depth 4\n   6. 192       blocked (a lane: 2 rows x 8 columns x 2 of k); B: 16 shuffles (unpacked); partial sums: 12 xor shuffles, depth 4\n  (30 more: mma ... all)\n  B-stationary: none possible: no assignment of the partial sums to registers (a xor of the lane's bits) lets a butterfly send and read them from the same registers in every lane\n  reference, each word fetched from the lane that holds it: 209 (output-stationary; A: 8 shuffles; B: 8 shuffles, depth 8); the chosen is 1.19x cheaper\n  chosen: output-stationary; A: 12 xor shuffles (unpacked); B: 16 shuffles (unpacked); k order by lane, cost 176\n    28 exchanges, 0 loads and 0 stores of shared memory (bank conflicts at most 1-way), 0 barriers, 6 unpacks, 32 multiply-adds, 0 adds\n    8 shuffle indices, 12 integer operations\n  proof: the plan run on symbols in all 32 lanes gives every element of D as exactly its 8 products and its C, each once (exhaustive over the lanes)\n  bound: |D - (A B + C)| <= gamma_8 (sum_k |A_ik B_kj| + |C_ij|), gamma_8 = 8 u / (1 - 8 u) = 4.768e-07, u = 2^-24\n    a product of two f16 is exact in f32 (22 significant bits, exponents within f32's normals), so only the sums round: each term through at most 8 roundings\n  holds when: every lane of the warp active, the warp a subgroup of 32 or 32 aligned lanes of a larger one; the f32 sums round to nearest\n  check: 64 random sets of fragments in f32 against the exact sums: within the bound, the largest error 0.59 of the bound (sampled, not a proof)\n  GLSL (mma_m16n8k8_f32.glsl):\n    // D = A B + C on a warp's fragments as PTX's mma.sync.aligned.m16n8k8.row.col\n    // lays them out (f16 A and B, f32 C and D), for a GPU without a matrix unit.\n    // ucas mma m16n8k8 f32 under gt1030: output-stationary; A: 12 xor shuffles (unpacked); B: 16 shuffles (unpacked); k order by lane;\n    // cost 176 (each word fetched from its lane: 209).\n    // Proved over the 32 lanes: each element of D is its 8 products and C, each once;\n    // |D - (A B + C)| <= gamma_8 (sum_k |A_ik B_kj| + |C_ij|), u = 2^-24.\n    #extension GL_KHR_shader_subgroup_basic : require\n    #extension GL_KHR_shader_subgroup_shuffle : require\n    void mma_m16n8k8_f32(uint a[2], uint b[1], float c[4], out float d[4])\n    {\n    \tuint lane = gl_SubgroupInvocationID & 31u;\n    \tuint base = gl_SubgroupInvocationID & ~31u;\n    \tfloat v0 = c[0];\n    \tfloat v1 = c[1];\n    \tfloat v2 = c[2];\n    \tfloat v3 = c[3];\n    \tuint v4 = a[0];\n    \tfloat v5 = unpackHalf2x16(v4).x;\n    \tuint v6 = b[0];\n    \tfloat v7 = unpackHalf2x16(v6).x;\n    \tuint i0 = base | ((lane & 3u) ^ ((lane & 3u) << 3u));\n    \tfloat v8 = subgroupShuffle(v7, i0);\n    \tfloat v9 = fma(v5, v8, v0);\n    \tfloat v10 = unpackHalf2x16(v4).y;\n    \tfloat v11 = unpackHalf2x16(v6).y;\n    \tfloat v12 = subgroupShuffle(v11, i0);\n    \tfloat v13 = fma(v10, v12, v9);\n    \tuint i1 = i0 ^ 4u;\n    \tfloat v14 = subgroupShuffle(v7, i1);\n    \tfloat v15 = fma(v5, v14, v1);\n    \tfloat v16 = subgroupShuffle(v11, i1);\n    \tfloat v17 = fma(v10, v16, v15);\n    \tuint v18 = a[1];\n    \tfloat v19 = unpackHalf2x16(v18).x;\n    \tfloat v20 = fma(v19, v8, v2);\n    \tfloat v21 = unpackHalf2x16(v18).y;\n    \tfloat v22 = fma(v21, v12, v20);\n    \tfloat v23 = fma(v19, v14, v3);\n    \tfloat v24 = fma(v21, v16, v23);\n    \tfloat v25 = subgroupShuffleXor(v5, 1u);\n    \tuint i3 = i0 ^ 1u;\n    \tfloat v26 = subgroupShuffle(v7, i3);\n    \tfloat v27 = fma(v25, v26, v13);\n    \tfloat v28 = subgroupShuffleXor(v10, 1u);\n    \tfloat v29 = subgroupShuffle(v11, i3);\n    \tfloat v30 = fma(v28, v29, v27);\n    \tuint i4 = i0 ^ 5u;\n    \tfloat v31 = subgroupShuffle(v7, i4);\n    \tfloat v32 = fma(v25, v31, v17);\n    \tfloat v33 = subgroupShuffle(v11, i4);\n    \tfloat v34 = fma(v28, v33, v32);\n    \tfloat v35 = subgroupShuffleXor(v19, 1u);\n    \tfloat v36 = fma(v35, v26, v22);\n    \tfloat v37 = subgroupShuffleXor(v21, 1u);\n    \tfloat v38 = fma(v37, v29, v36);\n    \tfloat v39 = fma(v35, v31, v24);\n    \tfloat v40 = fma(v37, v33, v39);\n    \tfloat v41 = subgroupShuffleXor(v5, 2u);\n    \tuint i6 = i0 ^ 2u;\n    \tfloat v42 = subgroupShuffle(v7, i6);\n    \tfloat v43 = fma(v41, v42, v30);\n    \tfloat v44 = subgroupShuffleXor(v10, 2u);\n    \tfloat v45 = subgroupShuffle(v11, i6);\n    \tfloat v46 = fma(v44, v45, v43);\n    \tuint i7 = i0 ^ 6u;\n    \tfloat v47 = subgroupShuffle(v7, i7);\n    \tfloat v48 = fma(v41, v47, v34);\n    \tfloat v49 = subgroupShuffle(v11, i7);\n    \tfloat v50 = fma(v44, v49, v48);\n    \tfloat v51 = subgroupShuffleXor(v19, 2u);\n    \tfloat v52 = fma(v51, v42, v38);\n    \tfloat v53 = subgroupShuffleXor(v21, 2u);\n    \tfloat v54 = fma(v53, v45, v52);\n    \tfloat v55 = fma(v51, v47, v40);\n    \tfloat v56 = fma(v53, v49, v55);\n    \tfloat v57 = subgroupShuffleXor(v5, 3u);\n    \tuint i9 = i0 ^ 3u;\n    \tfloat v58 = subgroupShuffle(v7, i9);\n    \tfloat v59 = fma(v57, v58, v46);\n    \tfloat v60 = subgroupShuffleXor(v10, 3u);\n    \tfloat v61 = subgroupShuffle(v11, i9);\n    \tfloat v62 = fma(v60, v61, v59);\n    \tuint i10 = i0 ^ 7u;\n    \tfloat v63 = subgroupShuffle(v7, i10);\n    \tfloat v64 = fma(v57, v63, v50);\n    \tfloat v65 = subgroupShuffle(v11, i10);\n    \tfloat v66 = fma(v60, v65, v64);\n    \tfloat v67 = subgroupShuffleXor(v19, 3u);\n    \tfloat v68 = fma(v67, v58, v54);\n    \tfloat v69 = subgroupShuffleXor(v21, 3u);\n    \tfloat v70 = fma(v69, v61, v68);\n    \tfloat v71 = fma(v67, v63, v56);\n    \tfloat v72 = fma(v69, v65, v71);\n    \td[0] = v62;\n    \td[1] = v66;\n    \td[2] = v70;\n    \td[3] = v72;\n    }\n  attached mma_m16n8k8_f32.glsl (3507 bytes)\n"}, {"type": "resource", "resource": {"uri": "ucas://file/mma_m16n8k8_f32.glsl", "mimeType": "text/plain", "blob": ""}}], "structuredContent": {"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "mma", "ucas": "mma m16n8k8", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "mma", "shape": "m16n8k8", "accumulator": "f32", "model": "gt1030", "tried": 1768, "dataflows": [{"cost": 176, "dataflow": "output-stationary; A: 12 xor shuffles (unpacked); B: 16 shuffles (unpacked); k order by lane", "depth": 8}, {"cost": 186, "dataflow": "output-stationary; A: 12 xor shuffles (unpacked); B: 8 shuffles; k order by lane", "depth": 8}, {"cost": 188, "dataflow": "output-stationary; A: 6 xor shuffles; B: 16 shuffles (unpacked); k order by lane", "depth": 8}, {"cost": 192, "dataflow": "A-stationary; B: 16 shuffles (unpacked); partial sums: 12 xor shuffles", "depth": 4}, {"cost": 192, "dataflow": "blocked (a lane: 2 rows x 8 columns x 2 of k); B: 16 shuffles (unpacked); partial sums: 12 xor shuffles", "depth": 4}, {"cost": 192, "dataflow": "blocked (a lane: 2 rows x 8 columns x 2 of k); B: 16 shuffles (unpacked); partial sums: 12 xor shuffles", "depth": 4}], "reference_cost": 209, "chosen": "output-stationary; A: 12 xor shuffles (unpacked); B: 16 shuffles (unpacked); k order by lane", "cost": 176, "bound": "gamma_8 (sum_k |A_ik B_kj| + |C_ij|)", "depth": 8, "glsl": "// D = A B + C on a warp's fragments as PTX's mma.sync.aligned.m16n8k8.row.col\n// lays them out (f16 A and B, f32 C and D), for a GPU without a matrix unit.\n// ucas mma m16n8k8 f32 under gt1030: output-stationary; A: 12 xor shuffles (unpacked); B: 16 shuffles (unpacked); k order by lane;\n// cost 176 (each word fetched from its lane: 209).\n// Proved over the 32 lanes: each element of D is its 8 products and C, each once;\n// |D - (A B + C)| <= gamma_8 (sum_k |A_ik B_kj| + |C_ij|), u = 2^-24.\n#extension GL_KHR_shader_subgroup_basic : require\n#extension GL_KHR_shader_subgroup_shuffle : require\nvoid mma_m16n8k8_f32(uint a[2], uint b[1], float c[4], out float d[4])\n{\n\tuint lane = gl_SubgroupInvocationID & 31u;\n\tuint base = gl_SubgroupInvocationID & ~31u;\n\tfloat v0 = c[0];\n\tfloat v1 = c[1];\n\tfloat v2 = c[2];\n\tfloat v3 = c[3];\n\tuint v4 = a[0];\n\tfloat v5 = unpackHalf2x16(v4).x;\n\tuint v6 = b[0];\n\tfloat v7 = unpackHalf2x16(v6).x;\n\tuint i0 = base | ((lane & 3u) ^ ((lane & 3u) << 3u));\n\tfloat v8 = subgroupShuffle(v7, i0);\n\tfloat v9 = fma(v5, v8, v0);\n\tfloat v10 = unpackHalf2x16(v4).y;\n\tfloat v11 = unpackHalf2x16(v6).y;\n\tfloat v12 = subgroupShuffle(v11, i0);\n\tfloat v13 = fma(v10, v12, v9);\n\tuint i1 = i0 ^ 4u;\n\tfloat v14 = subgroupShuffle(v7, i1);\n\tfloat v15 = fma(v5, v14, v1);\n\tfloat v16 = subgroupShuffle(v11, i1);\n\tfloat v17 = fma(v10, v16, v15);\n\tuint v18 = a[1];\n\tfloat v19 = unpackHalf2x16(v18).x;\n\tfloat v20 = fma(v19, v8, v2);\n\tfloat v21 = unpackHalf2x16(v18).y;\n\tfloat v22 = fma(v21, v12, v20);\n\tfloat v23 = fma(v19, v14, v3);\n\tfloat v24 = fma(v21, v16, v23);\n\tfloat v25 = subgroupShuffleXor(v5, 1u);\n\tuint i3 = i0 ^ 1u;\n\tfloat v26 = subgroupShuffle(v7, i3);\n\tfloat v27 = fma(v25, v26, v13);\n\tfloat v28 = subgroupShuffleXor(v10, 1u);\n\tfloat v29 = subgroupShuffle(v11, i3);\n\tfloat v30 = fma(v28, v29, v27);\n\tuint i4 = i0 ^ 5u;\n\tfloat v31 = subgroupShuffle(v7, i4);\n\tfloat v32 = fma(v25, v31, v17);\n\tfloat v33 = subgroupShuffle(v11, i4);\n\tfloat v34 = fma(v28, v33, v32);\n\tfloat v35 = subgroupShuffleXor(v19, 1u);\n\tfloat v36 = fma(v35, v26, v22);\n\tfloat v37 = subgroupShuffleXor(v21, 1u);\n\tfloat v38 = fma(v37, v29, v36);\n\tfloat v39 = fma(v35, v31, v24);\n\tfloat v40 = fma(v37, v33, v39);\n\tfloat v41 = subgroupShuffleXor(v5, 2u);\n\tuint i6 = i0 ^ 2u;\n\tfloat v42 = subgroupShuffle(v7, i6);\n\tfloat v43 = fma(v41, v42, v30);\n\tfloat v44 = subgroupShuffleXor(v10, 2u);\n\tfloat v45 = subgroupShuffle(v11, i6);\n\tfloat v46 = fma(v44, v45, v43);\n\tuint i7 = i0 ^ 6u;\n\tfloat v47 = subgroupShuffle(v7, i7);\n\tfloat v48 = fma(v41, v47, v34);\n\tfloat v49 = subgroupShuffle(v11, i7);\n\tfloat v50 = fma(v44, v49, v48);\n\tfloat v51 = subgroupShuffleXor(v19, 2u);\n\tfloat v52 = fma(v51, v42, v38);\n\tfloat v53 = subgroupShuffleXor(v21, 2u);\n\tfloat v54 = fma(v53, v45, v52);\n\tfloat v55 = fma(v51, v47, v40);\n\tfloat v56 = fma(v53, v49, v55);\n\tfloat v57 = subgroupShuffleXor(v5, 3u);\n\tuint i9 = i0 ^ 3u;\n\tfloat v58 = subgroupShuffle(v7, i9);\n\tfloat v59 = fma(v57, v58, v46);\n\tfloat v60 = subgroupShuffleXor(v10, 3u);\n\tfloat v61 = subgroupShuffle(v11, i9);\n\tfloat v62 = fma(v60, v61, v59);\n\tuint i10 = i0 ^ 7u;\n\tfloat v63 = subgroupShuffle(v7, i10);\n\tfloat v64 = fma(v57, v63, v50);\n\tfloat v65 = subgroupShuffle(v11, i10);\n\tfloat v66 = fma(v60, v65, v64);\n\tfloat v67 = subgroupShuffleXor(v19, 3u);\n\tfloat v68 = fma(v67, v58, v54);\n\tfloat v69 = subgroupShuffleXor(v21, 3u);\n\tfloat v70 = fma(v69, v61, v68);\n\tfloat v71 = fma(v67, v63, v56);\n\tfloat v72 = fma(v69, v65, v71);\n\td[0] = v62;\n\td[1] = v66;\n\td[2] = v70;\n\td[3] = v72;\n}\n"}, "notes": [], "conditions": ["every lane of the warp active, the warp a subgroup of 32 or 32 aligned lanes of a larger one", "the f32 sums round to nearest"], "checks": [{"kind": "random", "points": 8192, "max_diff": 0.5903529124498894, "passed": true, "text": "random fragments against the exact sums, as a fraction of the bound"}], "proof": {"kind": "exhaustive", "text": "the plan run on symbols in all 32 lanes: every element of D is exactly its K products and its C, each once"}, "files": [{"name": "mma_m16n8k8_f32.glsl", "mime": "text/plain", "bytes": 3507}], "text": "mma m16n8k8: D = A B + C on a warp's fragments as PTX's mma.sync.aligned.m16n8k8.row.col lays them out, f16 A and B, f32 C and D, 32 lanes, under gt1030 (1768 dataflows tried)\n  each of D's 128 elements is a sum of 8 products of f16 and its C\n   1. 176       output-stationary; A: 12 xor shuffles (unpacked); B: 16 shuffles (unpacked); k order by lane, depth 8\n   2. 186       output-stationary; A: 12 xor shuffles (unpacked); B: 8 shuffles; k order by lane, depth 8\n   3. 188       output-stationary; A: 6 xor shuffles; B: 16 shuffles (unpacked); k order by lane, depth 8\n   4. 192       A-stationary; B: 16 shuffles (unpacked); partial sums: 12 xor shuffles, depth 4\n   5. 192       blocked (a lane: 2 rows x 8 columns x 2 of k); B: 16 shuffles (unpacked); partial sums: 12 xor shuffles, depth 4\n   6. 192       blocked (a lane: 2 rows x 8 columns x 2 of k); B: 16 shuffles (unpacked); partial sums: 12 xor shuffles, depth 4\n  (30 more: mma ... all)\n  B-stationary: none possible: no assignment of the partial sums to registers (a xor of the lane's bits) lets a butterfly send and read them from the same registers in every lane\n  reference, each word fetched from the lane that holds it: 209 (output-stationary; A: 8 shuffles; B: 8 shuffles, depth 8); the chosen is 1.19x cheaper\n  chosen: output-stationary; A: 12 xor shuffles (unpacked); B: 16 shuffles (unpacked); k order by lane, cost 176\n    28 exchanges, 0 loads and 0 stores of shared memory (bank conflicts at most 1-way), 0 barriers, 6 unpacks, 32 multiply-adds, 0 adds\n    8 shuffle indices, 12 integer operations\n  proof: the plan run on symbols in all 32 lanes gives every element of D as exactly its 8 products and its C, each once (exhaustive over the lanes)\n  bound: |D - (A B + C)| <= gamma_8 (sum_k |A_ik B_kj| + |C_ij|), gamma_8 = 8 u / (1 - 8 u) = 4.768e-07, u = 2^-24\n    a product of two f16 is exact in f32 (22 significant bits, exponents within f32's normals), so only the sums round: each term through at most 8 roundings\n  holds when: every lane of the warp active, the warp a subgroup of 32 or 32 aligned lanes of a larger one; the f32 sums round to nearest\n  check: 64 random sets of fragments in f32 against the exact sums: within the bound, the largest error 0.59 of the bound (sampled, not a proof)\n  GLSL (mma_m16n8k8_f32.glsl):\n    // D = A B + C on a warp's fragments as PTX's mma.sync.aligned.m16n8k8.row.col\n    // lays them out (f16 A and B, f32 C and D), for a GPU without a matrix unit.\n    // ucas mma m16n8k8 f32 under gt1030: output-stationary; A: 12 xor shuffles (unpacked); B: 16 shuffles (unpacked); k order by lane;\n    // cost 176 (each word fetched from its lane: 209).\n    // Proved over the 32 lanes: each element of D is its 8 products and C, each once;\n    // |D - (A B + C)| <= gamma_8 (sum_k |A_ik B_kj| + |C_ij|), u = 2^-24.\n    #extension GL_KHR_shader_subgroup_basic : require\n    #extension GL_KHR_shader_subgroup_shuffle : require\n    void mma_m16n8k8_f32(uint a[2], uint b[1], float c[4], out float d[4])\n    {\n    \tuint lane = gl_SubgroupInvocationID & 31u;\n    \tuint base = gl_SubgroupInvocationID & ~31u;\n    \tfloat v0 = c[0];\n    \tfloat v1 = c[1];\n    \tfloat v2 = c[2];\n    \tfloat v3 = c[3];\n    \tuint v4 = a[0];\n    \tfloat v5 = unpackHalf2x16(v4).x;\n    \tuint v6 = b[0];\n    \tfloat v7 = unpackHalf2x16(v6).x;\n    \tuint i0 = base | ((lane & 3u) ^ ((lane & 3u) << 3u));\n    \tfloat v8 = subgroupShuffle(v7, i0);\n    \tfloat v9 = fma(v5, v8, v0);\n    \tfloat v10 = unpackHalf2x16(v4).y;\n    \tfloat v11 = unpackHalf2x16(v6).y;\n    \tfloat v12 = subgroupShuffle(v11, i0);\n    \tfloat v13 = fma(v10, v12, v9);\n    \tuint i1 = i0 ^ 4u;\n    \tfloat v14 = subgroupShuffle(v7, i1);\n    \tfloat v15 = fma(v5, v14, v1);\n    \tfloat v16 = subgroupShuffle(v11, i1);\n    \tfloat v17 = fma(v10, v16, v15);\n    \tuint v18 = a[1];\n    \tfloat v19 = unpackHalf2x16(v18).x;\n    \tfloat v20 = fma(v19, v8, v2);\n    \tfloat v21 = unpackHalf2x16(v18).y;\n    \tfloat v22 = fma(v21, v12, v20);\n    \tfloat v23 = fma(v19, v14, v3);\n    \tfloat v24 = fma(v21, v16, v23);\n    \tfloat v25 = subgroupShuffleXor(v5, 1u);\n    \tuint i3 = i0 ^ 1u;\n    \tfloat v26 = subgroupShuffle(v7, i3);\n    \tfloat v27 = fma(v25, v26, v13);\n    \tfloat v28 = subgroupShuffleXor(v10, 1u);\n    \tfloat v29 = subgroupShuffle(v11, i3);\n    \tfloat v30 = fma(v28, v29, v27);\n    \tuint i4 = i0 ^ 5u;\n    \tfloat v31 = subgroupShuffle(v7, i4);\n    \tfloat v32 = fma(v25, v31, v17);\n    \tfloat v33 = subgroupShuffle(v11, i4);\n    \tfloat v34 = fma(v28, v33, v32);\n    \tfloat v35 = subgroupShuffleXor(v19, 1u);\n    \tfloat v36 = fma(v35, v26, v22);\n    \tfloat v37 = subgroupShuffleXor(v21, 1u);\n    \tfloat v38 = fma(v37, v29, v36);\n    \tfloat v39 = fma(v35, v31, v24);\n    \tfloat v40 = fma(v37, v33, v39);\n    \tfloat v41 = subgroupShuffleXor(v5, 2u);\n    \tuint i6 = i0 ^ 2u;\n    \tfloat v42 = subgroupShuffle(v7, i6);\n    \tfloat v43 = fma(v41, v42, v30);\n    \tfloat v44 = subgroupShuffleXor(v10, 2u);\n    \tfloat v45 = subgroupShuffle(v11, i6);\n    \tfloat v46 = fma(v44, v45, v43);\n    \tuint i7 = i0 ^ 6u;\n    \tfloat v47 = subgroupShuffle(v7, i7);\n    \tfloat v48 = fma(v41, v47, v34);\n    \tfloat v49 = subgroupShuffle(v11, i7);\n    \tfloat v50 = fma(v44, v49, v48);\n    \tfloat v51 = subgroupShuffleXor(v19, 2u);\n    \tfloat v52 = fma(v51, v42, v38);\n    \tfloat v53 = subgroupShuffleXor(v21, 2u);\n    \tfloat v54 = fma(v53, v45, v52);\n    \tfloat v55 = fma(v51, v47, v40);\n    \tfloat v56 = fma(v53, v49, v55);\n    \tfloat v57 = subgroupShuffleXor(v5, 3u);\n    \tuint i9 = i0 ^ 3u;\n    \tfloat v58 = subgroupShuffle(v7, i9);\n    \tfloat v59 = fma(v57, v58, v46);\n    \tfloat v60 = subgroupShuffleXor(v10, 3u);\n    \tfloat v61 = subgroupShuffle(v11, i9);\n    \tfloat v62 = fma(v60, v61, v59);\n    \tuint i10 = i0 ^ 7u;\n    \tfloat v63 = subgroupShuffle(v7, i10);\n    \tfloat v64 = fma(v57, v63, v50);\n    \tfloat v65 = subgroupShuffle(v11, i10);\n    \tfloat v66 = fma(v60, v65, v64);\n    \tfloat v67 = subgroupShuffleXor(v19, 3u);\n    \tfloat v68 = fma(v67, v58, v54);\n    \tfloat v69 = subgroupShuffleXor(v21, 3u);\n    \tfloat v70 = fma(v69, v61, v68);\n    \tfloat v71 = fma(v67, v63, v56);\n    \tfloat v72 = fma(v69, v65, v71);\n    \td[0] = v62;\n    \td[1] = v66;\n    \td[2] = v70;\n    \td[3] = v72;\n    }\n  attached mma_m16n8k8_f32.glsl (3507 bytes)\n"}, "isError": false}}
